!
! Lines 12 and 13 print a DATA DESCRIPTION in the BINARY OUTPUT
! column, not machine code, and a SYN deposits nothing -- so they get
! !SYM lines and NO !CHECK, the convention printed pp.24, 98, 99 and
! 101 established.  Their "+" sign suffix is dropped in !SYM because
! listing_oracle compares a bit count.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------

!SYM KNEWT  221416.40
!SYM KREE   221420.40
!SYM KLABEL 221421.40
!SYM KKEXIT 221422.40
!SYM EIOIND 221370.00
!SYM EINDR  221371.00
!SYM KKSPAC 221424.00
!SYM RK1    221442.40
!SYM KSOSSP 221443.40
!
!CHECK 221415.40 | 000011.77 80 221274.34 00 | line 1 BZB,$R.63,K SOS -IF UK ALONE, MACHINE ERROR -- the first half word is the BIT ADDRESS $R.63, which reads $R as word 0o11 = 9 and the bit 0o77 = 63 exactly; the second is the branch to K SOS, landed at 221274.0 by printed p.125, and a branch shows only bit 32, so the .34 is operation bits and not an address reading. Line 45 is the same card and its check is the control on this one
!CHECK 221416.40 | 221614.00 80 | line 2 K NEW T SIC,J NEW T -- AN SIC CARRIES ITS OPERAND'S FULL 24-BIT BIT ADDRESS, so J NEW T is READ at 221614.00 to the bit. This row carries the first of the page's two location-column asterisks
!CHECK 221417.00 | 221541.10 00 | line 3 B,J NEW TE -IF UK + EOP, BAD TAPE -- target+.10 on J NEW TE's 221541.00; bit 32 is clear and the offset inside the half word is unobservable. The manuals spell JNEWTE 6 times and JNEWT once, which is what separates this symbol from line 2's
!CHECK 221417.40 | 000003.05 02 | line 4 LCI,2,3 -- a LITERAL count 3, no symbol; .05 is 2J+1 = 5 for J=2 and 02 is the LCI code. This row is the control for line 17, which runs the same operation with the same J against the SYMBOL K REP
!CHECK 221420.00 | 221406.50 00 | line 5 B,K R NEW -NEW TAPE IS READY -- 0o50 = 0o40 OR 0o10, so bit 32 IS SET and K R NEW is at 221406.40, not .00; that half word is the only part a plain B shows
!CHECK 221420.40 | 221405.44 48 | line 6 KREE CB,2,KRREAD.32 -- the ".32" is BARE DECIMAL and prints 0o40, then the CB adds its own 0o04, giving .44 on K RREAD's 221405.00. Line 46 is the same operation with the same J against a symbol on THIS page, so the two rows check the decimal-.32 rule against each other
!CHECK 221421.00 | 221416.50 00 | line 7 B,KNEWT -- >>> THIS ROW IS THE PAGE'S INTERNAL BACKSTOP. <<< KNEWT is line 2's own label at 221416.40, printed there with blanks as "K NEW T" and here CLOSED UP, and 0o50 = 0o40 OR 0o10 confirms the half word. Two spellings of one symbol on one page, agreeing in the compiled word
!CHECK 221421.40 | 221660.00 80 | line 8 K LABEL SIC,JWRITX -- SIC, so JWRITX is read at 221660.00 BIT-EXACT. The manuals spell JWRITX 3 times and JWRITL 8, and this page prints both (line 9), which is what tells them apart
!CHECK 221422.00 | 221622.10 00 | line 9 B,JWRITL -RETRY WRITE LABEL -- target+.10 on 221622.00; bit offset unobservable
!CHECK 221422.40 | 000000.00 80 010000.00 70 | line 10 K K EXIT C0000(BU,8),, -- A CONNECTIVE WITH BOTH OPERANDS EMPTY. The four binary digits of the mnemonic are PRINTED in the second half word (C0001 gives .02, C0010 .04, C0100 .10, C1000 .20), so this check reads all four and is not a tautology; 0o010000 is the (BU,8) dds, length 8, and 70 is the connective code
!CHECK 221423.40 | 221371.10 00 | line 11 B,K K IND -- target+.10 on K K IND's 221371.00, which is the SAME WORD line 13 aliases as E IND R. The page therefore states that address twice, once as a branch target and once as a SYN value
!CHECK 221424.00 | 000036.05 02 | line 17 K K SPAC LCI,2,K REP -- K REP is the COUNT 30 (0o36), landed by printed p.125 which prints this identical half word five times with other J values; .05 is 2J+1 for J=2, matching line 4's literal
!CHECK 221424.40 | 000136.05 01 | line 18 LVI,2,(8)136. -REWIND TAPE -- the I-O CONTROL CODE 0o136, Rewind, loaded as an immediate value; the same J=2 .05 as lines 4 and 17 but with the LVI code 01 instead of LCI's 02, so the two operations are each other's control
!CHECK 221425.00 | 221475.00 10 | line 19 LX,C,K CTL CM -- the printed "C" is an INDEX REGISTER NUMBER and the compiled .00 is 2J for J=0, which is what settles it (line 33's LV,1 prints .02 for J=1). The 10 is the LX code. K CTL CM's bit offset is unobservable and its SPELLING is open, see note (A)
!CHECK 221425.40 | 221502.00 80 | line 20 SIC,K SEOP R -- SIC, so 221502.00 is read to the bit. Line 30 is the same card and compiles the same word
!CHECK 221426.00 | 221476.10 00 | line 21 B,K K EOP -- target+.10 on 221476.00. The name's middle letter is settled by line 23's comment "-WAIT FOR END OP REW", which spells it in English
!CHECK 221426.40 | 221325.40 80 | line 22 SIC,K UNR R -- SIC, BIT-EXACT at 221325.40 INCLUDING the .40. The statement prints "K LNR R" because the U loses its right stem on this drum; printed p.184 line 22 is the same card at the same address and printed p.186 line 30 is the defining card, so the U is not a guess
!CHECK 221427.00 | 221321.50 00 | line 23 B,K K LOOP -WAIT FOR END OP REW -- 0o50 confirms bit 32, so K K LOOP is at 221321.40; printed p.184 line 23 is the same card and printed p.186 line 24 is the defining card
!CHECK 221427.40 | 221313.40 80 | line 24 SIC,K CBJ R -- SIC, BIT-EXACT at 221313.40; printed p.184 line 24 is the same card and printed p.186 line 9 defines it
!CHECK 221430.00 | 221302.50 00 | line 25 B,K CLEAR -CLEAR CONTROL WORD -- 0o50 confirms K CLEAR's bit 32, matching printed p.184 line 25
!CHECK 221430.40 | 000000.03 01 | line 26 LVI,1,S INST D -SET UNIT TO INSTALLATION DENS -- S INST D is printed p.108 line 6's "SYN(BU,24),0.0", so the whole address field is zero and .03 is 2J+1 = 3 for J=1; printed pp.162 and 183 compile the identical row with J=0 and print .01, which is what makes the J field readable here
!CHECK 221431.00 | 221474.40 80 | line 27 SIC,K DEN OK -- SIC, BIT-EXACT at 221474.40 including the .40. Line 34 is the same card; the D is settled by rung 4 against line 34's open print
!CHECK 221431.40 | 221466.10 00 | line 28 B,K K DENS -- target+.10 on 221466.00; the D is settled by rung 4 against line 35, and KKDENS has 5 typeset hits
!CHECK 221432.00 | 000076.05 01 | line 29 LVI,2,(8)76. -SPACEBLOCK -- the I-O control code 0o76; the same J=2 .05 and LVI code 01 as line 18 with a different literal, so the pair pins the literal. This row carries the page's second location-column asterisk
!CHECK 221432.40 | 221502.00 80 | line 30 SIC,K SEOP R -- the same card as line 20, compiling the same word; the page prints this statement twice
!CHECK 221433.00 | 221476.10 00 | line 31 B,K K EOP -- the same card as line 21
!CHECK 221433.40 | 000002.33 8D 001027.20 50 | line 32 L(BU,1),S F DEN($13),46 -SET UNIT TO FILE DENSITY -- >>> A VFL OPERAND READS ITS SYMBOL TO THE BIT. <<< S F DEN is printed p.102 line 12's "SYN(BU,2),2.27" and 2.27 DECIMAL is word 2 bit 27 = 0o33, which is the whole of the first address, so this row CHECKS the bit offset and not just the word. 8D's low nibble is the named index $13; the second word carries the statement's OWN (BU,1) -- length 1, not the symbol's 2 -- plus the offset 46 and the L code 50
!CHECK 221434.40 | 000011.02 30 | line 33 LV,1,$R -- $R resolves to word 0o11 = 9, the SAME word lines 1 and 45 address as $R.63, through a different operation; .02 is 2J for J=1 and 30 is the LV code
!CHECK 221435.00 | 221474.40 80 | line 34 SIC,K DEN OK -- the same card as line 27
!CHECK 221435.40 | 221466.10 00 | line 35 B,K K DENS -- the same card as line 28
!CHECK 221436.00 | 000077.05 01 | line 36 LVI,2,(8)77. -RETRY SPACEFILE -- the third control code on the page, 0o77, in the same shape as lines 18 and 29
!CHECK 221436.40 | 221512.40 80 | line 37 SIC,K K RET -- SIC, BIT-EXACT at 221512.40 including the .40; the manuals spell KKRET 6 times
!CHECK 221437.00 | 221505.10 00 | line 38 B,K IO REJ -- target+.10 on 221505.00; the round glyph is settled by the manuals, KIOREJ 7 against KICREJ 3, the same split that settles K IO IND on line 12
!CHECK 221437.40 | 221440.43 01 | line 39 LVI,1,$+1.0 -- SELF-RELATIVE and therefore a check on the page's own counter: $ is 221437.40, $+1.0 is 221440.40, and 0o43 = 0o40 OR 2J+1 for J=1. If the arrival at line 39 were wrong by a word this check would fail
!CHECK 221440.00 | 221525.10 00 | line 40 B,J SEOP T -CHECK TERMINATION -- target+.10 on 221525.00; the manuals spell JSEOPT 5 times against JSECPT once, which is also what settles the four shared glyphs of K SEOP R on lines 20 and 30
!CHECK 221440.40 | 221443.50 00 | line 41 B,K SOS SP -EPGK - GIVE UP AFTER 3 TRIES -- K SOS SP is THIS page's line 46 at 221443.40 and 0o50 confirms bit 32, so this is a real address check on a label the page defines
!CHECK 221441.00 | 221442.50 00 | line 42 B,RK1 -- RK1 is THIS page's line 45 at 221442.40
!CHECK 221441.40 | 221422.50 00 | line 43 B,K K EXIT -EE - SUCCESSFUL END -- K K EXIT is THIS page's line 10 at 221422.40. Line 44 is the same card with a different comment, and the two prints of "EXIT" in the same character positions are what settle the E
!CHECK 221442.00 | 221422.50 00 | line 44 B,K K EXIT -EOP - IMPOSSIBLE -- identical to line 43, different comment
!CHECK 221442.40 | 000011.77 80 221274.34 00 | line 45 RK1 BZB,$R.63,K SOS -- the same card as line 1, and the page's cleanest rung-4 pair: both prints of "SOS" sit in the same character positions
!CHECK 221443.40 | 221424.44 48 | line 46 K SOS SP CB,2,K K SPAC.32 -- the ".32" is bare decimal and prints 0o40, plus the CB's own 0o04, on K K SPAC's 221424.00 -- THIS page's line 17. So the decimal-.32 rule, the CB byte 48 and the label are all checked together, and line 6 computes the same shape against an external
!CHECK 221444.00 | 221274.10 00 | line 47 B,K SOS -- target+.10 on K SOS's 221274.00, the same symbol lines 1 and 45 branch to; printed p.125 line 31 prints this identical half word. This is the page's LAST row, so the counter leaves at 221444.40
